-- s 139(2): the lesser of 10 penalty units and one fifth of the maximum (s 22(2): 60 / 5 = 12, so 10).
#ASSERT `What is the most an infringement notice can charge` `s 22(2) employer's duty to keep records and engage advisers` `a natural person` TRUE EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `What is the most an infringement notice can charge` `s 35 duty to consult` `a body corporate` TRUE EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `What is the most an infringement notice can charge` `s 35 duty to consult` `a natural person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the most an infringement notice can charge` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` `a natural person` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the most an infringement notice can charge` `s 38 incident notification and record` `a body corporate` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ss 148A, 148B.
#ASSERT `Can insurance pay the penalty` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can insurance pay the penalty` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The s 38(3) rule itself (clock: hours from the duty to notify).
#TRACE `s 38(3) -- the written record of the incident within 48 hours` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the duty-holder` DOES `give the Authority a written record of the incident` AT 47
-- expect: FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 38(3) -- the written record of the incident within 48 hours` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Authority` DOES `wait` AT 49
-- expect: BREACH BY `the duty-holder` (no record within 48 hours)
